00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.269
And basically my whole family is convinced
the world's about that.

00:00:29.269 --> 00:00:30.269
OK.

00:00:30.269 --> 00:00:33.110
And I want to know, do you have a doomsday
plan?

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.920
And is it even worth it to form a doomsday
plan?

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:36.920
OK.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:37.920
Good.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.510
So just so I understand, Sam, is your family
of a particular religious faith?

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:44.730
Oh, yeah, sure, buddy.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:45.730
It's fine.

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:50.431
But those are the ones who are the ones who
are most into prepping are not extra religious.

00:00:50.431 --> 00:00:51.431
But I do come from a Catholic family.

00:00:51.431 --> 00:00:52.431
Oh, okay.

00:00:52.431 --> 00:00:53.431
All right.

00:00:53.431 --> 00:00:54.431
That's interesting.

00:00:54.431 --> 00:00:55.649
And then we're in the country.

00:00:55.649 --> 00:00:58.820
Is this all happening?

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.380
So my family lives in South Dakota.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:05.880
These are the bunkers apparently in Montana
and I live in Texas.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:06.880
And did you not?

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.049
You knew about the existence of this bunker
writers?

00:01:09.049 --> 00:01:10.049
What was the news of?

00:01:10.049 --> 00:01:13.600
It also knew oh, it was news once we got that
phone call.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.920
Oh, you didn't even know your family had this
bunker.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.020
I know.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:18.740
I do not know.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:22.560
So I've learned a lot of things in a few days
and they're apparently like getting it ready.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:23.560
Wow.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:24.560
So listen here.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:25.560
Here's my view.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.719
I do believe it makes sense to have to do
basic preparedness.

00:01:27.719 --> 00:01:33.560
And we've interviewed a couple of preparedness
experts and their view tends to be it doesn't

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:39.759
really make sense to plan for the events that
sort of have never happened and aren't like

00:01:39.759 --> 00:01:42.799
in the reasonable scope of what what you can
kind of plan for.

00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:48.369
It makes sense to plan for more likely things
so you can't leave your house at all for three

00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:54.630
days or the food supplies interrupted for
a couple of weeks or something like that.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:02:00.630
So from everything I've read, the most reasonable
thing to do is to have some some amount of

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:06.270
first aid supplies, certainly nonperishable
food that would last a couple of weeks in

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:10.200
a stock that you're not regularly using, you
know, to feed yourself.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:16.719
And, you know, certainly now people are thinking
it makes sense to have some masks, some N-95

00:02:16.719 --> 00:02:17.719
masks.

00:02:17.719 --> 00:02:20.319
When this is all done, I'm sure there will
be a lot of people that are going to debate

00:02:20.319 --> 00:02:21.569
basic preparedness.

00:02:21.569 --> 00:02:27.250
But, you know, saying everyone should have
a Montana bunker with three years of food.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:31.739
I mean, first of all, it's laughably unaffordable
for the vast majority of the country, number

00:02:31.739 --> 00:02:32.739
one.

00:02:32.739 --> 00:02:37.420
Now, that's not a reason not to do it, but
it seems from the survival experts I've spoken

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:41.299
to that that's probably more than what really
is logical.

00:02:41.299 --> 00:02:44.189
Are you.

00:02:44.189 --> 00:02:51.170
Are you telling me that amassing like 40 guns
and the like, 30 gallons of rice and sticking

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:55.730
it in a hole in the middle of nowhere is not
it's not like a logical thing.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:03:00.359
That may not be the most logical thing I've
ever heard of.

00:03:00.359 --> 00:03:01.909
Right.

00:03:01.909 --> 00:03:05.219
But but but, you know, once it hits the fan,
once things actually do crumble, you're gonna

00:03:05.219 --> 00:03:07.170
be like, gosh, I wish I had that bunker.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:08.170
I don't know.

00:03:08.170 --> 00:03:09.629
I mean, no, listen, it's completely true.

00:03:09.629 --> 00:03:13.629
Like, so about a year and a half ago, I did
some disaster preparedness.

00:03:13.629 --> 00:03:18.629
And I. I have kids that are in both of both
of the cars that my girlfriend that I have.

00:03:18.629 --> 00:03:20.400
And then we've got some supplies at home.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:25.180
And then we've built up kind of our non-perishables
in a very, very reasonable way.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.980
And I think that a lot more people are going
to be doing that.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:33.069
And now, I mean, listen, I'm keeping a list
of things that once things settle down, if

00:03:33.069 --> 00:03:37.830
I survive all of this, I want to to have just
to feel, OK, so like, for example, now that

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:44.200
we know about the run on masks, okay, maybe
I'll get 20 masks or, you know, 50 masks or

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:48.069
some number and have them for whenever, just
so I don't have to worry about it.

00:03:48.069 --> 00:03:49.069
Right.

00:03:49.069 --> 00:03:50.969
I put it out of my head, so to speak, or whatever.

00:03:50.969 --> 00:03:56.629
I think that we're going to see more people
certainly do that once this all settles down.

00:03:56.629 --> 00:04:00.540
Yeah, and then but certainly the smart thing.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:06.300
And so I definitely wish you luck if society
does crumble, I hope that you're able to find

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.300
a Montana bunker.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.300
Thank you.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.300
All right.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.300
Very good.

